cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus build, these tests or the prediction registry, please cite it as below."
title: "Indus script: a reproducible decipherment attempt"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible structural and functional analysis of the Indus script. It covers a corpus build of
  Mahadevan 1977 and the Wells/Fuls ICIT, held-out tests on a leak-free family split, a red-team
  reimplementation, a project-wide multiple-testing ledger, an atlas of closed routes and a
  hash-sealed registry of predictions for future finds. The result is a partial decipherment at the
  levels of structure (L0) and function (L1). There is no phonetic reading, and the language is not
  identified.
type: software
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
authors:
